window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["vw/transporter-t6"]={"transporter-t6-activate-daytime-running-lights-drl-only-with-headlight-switch-in-auto-position":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate daytime running lights (DRL) only when the light <strong>switch</strong> is in Auto position.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>26</strong>: <br/>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Light (DRL) only active with Assistance Driving Light (ADL) active”.  </p>","transporter-t6-activate-off-road-mode-on-discover-pq":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add Offroad mode to Discover PQ with navigation.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 3 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_List_BAP_Gen2-compass_0x15</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass_over-threshold_high</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>Restart the Discover Media PQ (hold down the ON/OFF button for at least 5 seconds).</p>\n<p>Depending on your hardware and firmware, the off-road menu may appear directly in the Menu, or it may be hidden:<br/>Press the VOICE-MENU-NAV buttons to access the secret menu, where you’ll now find the OFFROAD screen:  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroadpq-1024x768-39023fd7.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroadmenupq-1024x619-dc3e8b4c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroad-1024x631-441bee99.webp\"/></figure>","transporter-t6-activate-rearview-camera-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the reversing camera after installation for Discover PQ (retrofit).  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte <strong>19</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>4</strong> to “Rear View Camera (RVC) Low installed (PR-KA1).”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/C25A41FA-66F7-4FC9-B7F4-1761395A1D01-1024x483-11bbd3cf.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Optional, if parking assist is available)</strong> <strong>:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>10 – Parking Assistance</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>02</strong><br/>. Then, for bits <strong>4-5</strong>, select<em> “10 Camera Type: Rear View Camera (RVC) installed.”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Hardware upgrade :</strong></p>\n<p>The camera’s video cable is connected to the infotainment control unit. It is installed in the glovebox.   <br/><br/>The 2 pins of the reversing camera are used in the 12-pin quadlock (blue). Usable cable set: Part no. 000 979 009 E <br/><br/>Quadblock Assignment :<br/><br/>Pin 6 = video line<br/>Pin 12 = shielding</p>","transporter-t6-activate-the-discover-hidden-menu":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates the green hidden menu (green menu, hidden menu, testmode, engineer mode) on Discover MIB2.  </p>\n<p>/!\\ Caution: Making certain changes in the hidden menu may cause MIB2 to freeze or no longer start /!\\<br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“S12345</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Developer mode</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the value<strong>“activated</strong>”.</p>\n<p><em>Restart MIB2, keep MENU button pressed until testmode menu appears</em><br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/developermode-bfa51f40.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/developermode2-1024x576-7a0c833c.webp\"/></figure>","transporter-t6-activating-coming-leaving-home":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Activates Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>10</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Coming-Home (CH) active”<br/>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Leaving-Home (CH) active”.</p>","transporter-t6-add-daytime-running-lights-drl-to-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add daytime running light (DRL) activation/deactivation to the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>12</strong>: Bit <strong>1</strong>: Tick “Daytime Running Light (DRL) adjustable (Manually AND/OR Instrument Cluster)”.</p>","transporter-t6-automatic-door-locks":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Enables automatic door locking at speeds over 15km/h to be set. <br/><br/><em>Information: If auto-lock doesn’t work, deactivate and reactivate coding with hood open. </em> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Channel 03 (Auto-Lock drop-down list) <em>Set value to <strong>1</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 If the adaptation channel is not enabled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4 : </strong> Check “Auto-Lock active”. </em> </p>","transporter-t6-automatic-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to set automatic door unlocking when the key is removed.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> Channel 04 (drop-down list (Auto-Unlock)) <em>Set value to <strong>1</strong></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw-door-unlock-798a1163.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 If the adaptation channel is not enabled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Plant.</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0 : </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Auto-Unlock active”. </em> </p>","transporter-t6-automatic-headlamps-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte 0 Bit 0: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","transporter-t6-automatic-headlight-activation-in-the-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to automatically turn on the lights when it’s raining and the wipers have been triggered.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte 0 Bit 1: Check “Rain Light Function Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","transporter-t6-comfort-turn-signal":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the number of flashes for the “Comfort flashing” option.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Comfort Turn Signal</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – Choose between “<strong>1</strong>” and “<strong>5</strong>,” then confirm.</p>","transporter-t6-corner-lights-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activating the <strong>turn signals</strong> causes the fog light on the side toward which you’re turning the steering wheel to turn on when traveling at speeds below 50 km/h. This feature is also called “cornering lights.” Once this feature is activated, the fog light on the side of the turn you’re making will turn on! It’s super handy on narrow roads or in roundabouts.     </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Control Unit</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4-Activation-des-feux-en-virage-sur-Golf-5-et-6-f4e51c90.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select  </p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>12</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Cornering Light Activation Time Limited”</em></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>14: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7: </strong> Check “Cornering Lights via Front Fog Lights active”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5-Activation-de-la-fonction-Cornering-Lights-via-F-255e876b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – After completing this step, click on the “Exit” menu<br/>, then click “OK.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6-Activation-de-la-fonction-Cornering-Lights-via-F-2a08cc40.webp\"/></figure>","transporter-t6-cruise-control-activation-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to activate GRA cruise control (retrofit). </p>\n<p><strong>Modification only possible after retrofitting cruise control switch and <a href=\"https://wiki.ross-tech.com/wiki/index.php/Steering_Wheel_Control_Module_Versions\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">check that your multifunction steering wheel is compatible (midline or highline)</a>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>01 – Motor</strong> “.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on ” <strong>Coding II (11) or Login 11</strong> “. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur1-1c279499.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Then enter code <strong>11463</strong>, then <strong>OK</strong> (Do It!)</p>\n<p>The code 11463 is used to <strong>activate</strong> the controller, to <strong>deactivate</strong> it if necessary the code is 16167.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur2-6871f13e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>16 – Multifunction handwheel</strong> “.<br/><br/>4<strong>– </strong>Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong> “. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur3-945b80f3.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Options: We note in the penultimate section (0xxxx<strong>?</strong>x):<br/><br/>0 = No regulator installed (CCS not installed)<br/>1 = Regulator installed with 6 positions on a separate switch (CCS with 6 positions …. etc)<br/>3 = Regulator installed with 4 positions on the blinker switch (CCS with 4 positions via Blinker Stalk)</p>\n<p>So replace the “<strong>?</strong>” with the 3 for commodo regulator.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”, then click on ” Select</strong> “. <strong><strong>01 – Engine</strong></strong> ” .<br/><br/>4 – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select byte<strong>“5</strong>“<br/>Check bit<strong>“5</strong>” Cruise Control System (CCS) installed</p>\n<p>Or byte <strong>6</strong> bit <strong>0</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur5-1024x491-af7739d1.webp\"/></figure>","transporter-t6-daytime-running-lights-off-drl-with-handbrake-on":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to deactivate the daytime running lights (DRL) when the handbrake is engaged.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: If this is a hidden bit, replace the last <strong>0</strong> on the right side of the binary number with <strong>a 1</strong>. (<strong>10001000</strong> =&gt; <strong>10001001</strong>)</em></p>","transporter-t6-deactivate-mirrorlink":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable or remove MirrorLink from App-Connect on the MIB Discover PQ. The MirrorLink service has not been natively available on Android since June 1, 2020. For a direct connection to Android Auto.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicle configuration-Mirror_link</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Disabled</strong>” and confirm.</p>","transporter-t6-delete-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>1: </strong>“<strong>Seatbelt warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","transporter-t6-disable-am-frequency-on-discover":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to disable the AM radio frequency on the Discover PQ (AM radio frequency is rarely used, unlike FM radio frequency).  </p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>14</strong></p>\n<p>Set bit <strong>1</strong> <strong>“AM_disable</strong></p>\n<figure>\n</figure>","transporter-t6-disable-plate-lighting-control-odb-led-error":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Disables license plate light control. Useful when installing LED bulbs without resistance or for error prevention.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Bytes <strong>23</strong>:  </p>\n<p>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Uncheck: “Lamp Monitoring (Cold) License Plate Lamps Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/led_plaque5-odt_147-d36567c5.webp\"/></figure>","transporter-t6-door-lock-unlock-confirmation-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Enables vehicle lock/unlock confirmation with beeps (with alarm)  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong> Select Byte <strong>5</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation via Horn Enabled”</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>4: </strong> Check “Unlocking Confirmation via Horn active” </p>","transporter-t6-enable-usb-port-for-iphone-carplay-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the USB port for iPhone CarPlay accounting (after activating App Connect and changing the USB and/or USB cable) for Discover MIB2 PQ (2015). (Retrofit) </p>\n<p>For firmware references: <br/>MST2_EU_VW_PQ_P02XXT</p>\n<p>Modify the MIB2 coding and adaptation to recognize the new USB port (USB connector ref 5Q0 035 726 E) for both CarPlay and USB multimedia playback. A coding pin on the connector needs to be modified.  </p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/app-connect-carplay-activation\">–&gt; App Connect Activation for CarPlay and Android Auto</a><br/><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/prise-usb-aux-vw-golf-7-carplay-media-mib2-5q0-035-726-e/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">–&gt; USB/AUX Port for VW Golf 7 CarPlay Media MIB2 5Q0 035 726 E on VAG Custom</a></strong><br/><a href=\"#/vw/transporter-t6/transporter-t6-deactivate-mirrorlink\"><strong>–&gt; Disable MirrorLink</strong></a><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Codage- 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Assistant Codage Long</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5 </strong>– Select byte<strong>“19</strong>“<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“6-7</strong>” (C0 USB Configuration: USB and iPhone Functionality)<br/><br/><strong>Ligne 2 <strong>(optional)</strong> :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “<strong><strong>Interface for external media activation – connection 1</strong></strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the value “<strong><strong>activated</strong></strong>“<br/><br/><br/></p>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/activation-app-connect-pour-volkswagen/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activation APP CONNECT pour Volkswagen</a></blockquote>\n</figure>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/prise-usb-aux-vw-golf-7-carplay-media-mib2-5q0-035-726-e/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Prise USB / AUX VW Golf 7 CarPlay Media MIB2 5Q0 035 726 E</a></blockquote>\n</figure>","transporter-t6-flash-mode-lights-during-emergency-braking":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the brake/turn signal lights in flash mode during emergency braking.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>12</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Brake Light active” (to activate brake lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Turn Signal active” (to activate turn signals)</em></p>","transporter-t6-lower-passenger-mirror-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically lowers the passenger mirror when reversing.  </p>\n<p>The mirror adjustment knob must be in position<strong>“R”</strong> for the passenger mirror to lower automatically.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>09 – Centrale Elec</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf61-d4a12d4d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf62-a22a3a65.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the window that appears, select byte<strong> 4</strong> and check bit <strong>3 “</strong> <strong>Mirror Lowering With Reverse Rear </strong>” to activate mirror lowering when shifting into reverse gear:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf63-d65eea5e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– After this operation, click on the “Output” menu, then validate “OK”.  </p>\n<p>A message appears to inform you that the coding has been accepted.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:  </strong></p>\n<p><strong>3 –</strong> Click on<strong> “Select” </strong>, then click on<strong> “52 – Passenger door”.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><em>Add <strong>256</strong> to the value</em></p>","transporter-t6-memory-for-heated-seats":"<p><strong>How it works :</strong> When you switch on the heated seat(s), as soon as you remove the key from the ignition the setting is immediately switched off. With this activation, when you switch the ignition back on, the seat will have returned to the level at which you left it.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“08 – Climatronic</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose  </p>\n<p>“<strong>Retention of driver’s seat heater level</strong>” for <strong>Driver’s seat heater memory</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3AA-907-044-AG_Module08_Adaptation_retention_of_dr-51646659.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>and/or<strong>“Retention of passenger’s seat heater level</strong>” for <strong>Passenger seat heater memory</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3AA-907-044-AG_Module08_Adaptation_retention_of_pa-61b11e06.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>6</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>","transporter-t6-mute-push-to-talk-button":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Allows you to change the Push-To-Talk (PTT) button on the bottom left of your multifunction steering wheel, to act as a mute button for sound volume.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>16 – Multifunction Steering Wheel.”</strong><br/></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding- 07</strong>”. then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select <em>Byte<strong> 1</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck </em><em>“Multi-Function-Steering-Wheel (MFSW) with Push-To-Talk (PPT) Button installed</em>”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/pttg6-da3300eb.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>The Push-to-Talk (PPT) button now acts as a mute button.</p>","transporter-t6-needle-check":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> activates needle sweep when the car is started. (Needle Sweep)   <br/></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>10-Adaptation</strong>” then in the window that appears, click on the drop-down menu to choose a channel and select the “<strong>Staging</strong>” channel, if unavailable select the “<strong>indicator_celebration</strong>” channel:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg6-9456b738.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the “<strong>New value</strong>” box, click on the drop-down menu and select “<strong>active</strong>”. Once this new value has been entered, click on “<strong>Save</strong>”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg62-c8918051.webp\"/></figure>","transporter-t6-opening-closing-windows-with-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate closing and opening of the windows and sunroof with the remote control <strong>WITHOUT </strong>remaining pressed until the windows are completely closed.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><em> </em><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect. </strong></strong> “.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click <strong>“Encoding 07</strong>,” then “Long Coding Helper”</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> <em>Byte <strong>3</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Check “<em>Comfort Operation via Remote Control Active</em>”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7790-dfc7ad77.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Bit 0 – <em>Comfort Opening for Sliding Roof Active</em> will also open the sunroof while opening the windows by remote control.</p>\n<p><em>Pressing the remote control’s close button for 3 seconds will first lock the doors and then close the windows, without having to keep the button pressed until they are fully closed</em>.</p>","transporter-t6-refuel-quantity-display-on-the-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Displays the amount of fuel needed to completely fill your tank on the OBD (On-Board Computer). <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10” </strong>.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>“Volume to be Replenished” </strong>from the value list.</p>\n<p>Select ” <strong>Yes</strong> ” in the second value list.</p>","transporter-t6-selective-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to configure selective door unlocking.  </p>\n<p>When unlocking the vehicle, only the driver’s door is unlocked. To unlock all doors, press the remote control’s unlock button twice.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Channel 06 (drop-down list : Selective (Single) Door Locking) <em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 If the adaptation channel is not enabled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Plant.</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 0 </strong>: Check “Selective Central Locking active (Single Door Locking)”. </em> </p>","transporter-t6-start-stop-deactivation":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To completely deactivate the Start/Stop. <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 1 (via temperature) :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Long Adaptation – 0A”</strong>.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select Channel<strong>“13</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – In new value, select<strong>“D02000</strong>” (default value = <strong>002000</strong>) then validate.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/gof6startstop-1024x528-699ec970.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Line 2 (If line 1 didn’t work.) :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“61 – Battery Regul.</strong><br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Long Adaptation – 0A”</strong>.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select Channel<strong>“15</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – In new value, select<strong>“3D</strong>” (default value = <strong>10</strong>) then validate.</p>"};
